      "Evidence": "Terms like \u0027CorpoNations,\u0027 \u0027GLMZ,\u0027 \u0027neuretics,\u0027 \u0027Splicer,\u0027 \u0027\u03A6\u0027 (currency), \u0027Praxis,\u0027 \u0027Carrion,\u0027 and \u0027the Ghost Period\u0027 are dropped in with zero orientation \u2014 e.g. \u0027the CorpoNation property registry sometime in the 2190s\u0027 or \u0027GLMZ night\u0027 assumes the reader already knows what these zones/factions are, and later terms like \u0027Atlas NeoCortex,\u0027 \u0027the sixty-four,\u0027 and \u0027the aperture\u0027 pile up in dense lore-exposition paragraphs that read as pure info-dump rather than in-voice gloss.",
      "Fix": "Introduce each proprietary term through a concrete sensory or functional detail the first time Kyle\u0027s POV encounters it (as was done reasonably well with \u0027schism\u0027 and \u0027the array\u0027), and cut or redistribute the late-manuscript exposition blocks (e.g. the Atlas NeoCortex/sixty-four splices explanation) into smaller, scene-grounded beats rather than standalone lecture paragraphs."
